# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE FIRST ENTRY IS THE IMPORTANT ONE.
#
# safety/patterns.local.json holds the operator's DENIED VALUES — the exact strings that must never
# reach this public repository. If it were committed, this repo would publish a machine-readable
# index of precisely what is being protected, which is the opposite of the point. It is generated
# from the private control workspace and it never leaves it.
#
# safety/verify_publish_safe.cjs FAILS CLOSED when this file is missing. It does not fall back to
# "structural checks only" — a gate that quietly drops its teeth produces a green tick that means
# nothing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
safety/patterns.local.json

# Anything that has ever been a leak vector in this estate, refused by name as well as by the gate.
**/session-history/
*.env
.env*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
**/OPERATIONS_MANUAL*
**/operator-decisions.y*ml
**/REQUEST-TO-JULES*

# Build + tooling
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
.vercel/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
.safety-mutation-fixture/

# Generated content is committed deliberately (the site must build without the private repos),
# but the generator's scratch space is not.
.generator-cache/

# Absolute paths map the operator's filesystem. Same rule as the denylist: local only.
generators/roots.local.json
